# The alternating cases of the marked parabolic in 13.5.21

The six-letter branch proves the bound for the original seed in K*T* and
identifies the exact local product and two-residual. The quotient used for
natural coordinates is the literal quotient by the K*-fixed vectors.

Full linear displacement is also transported to the literal tilde-group
commutator, with its representative formulas retained.

Assembly of the eight-letter calculation and whole-module L₁-generation
remains here. No completed claim of 13.5.21(6) is made.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.5.21, final paragraph, printed p.924 (PDF p.941).
-/
